      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T03:03:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[AI] Nit: `pipe()` followed by `SetCloseOnExec()` isn\u0027t atomic. Another thread forking for its own `exec_script()` in between would leak `exec_write` into that child, and this `read()` would block until it exits. `pipe2(exec_fd, O_CLOEXEC)` where available would close the window.",
      "revId": "c54eba3f2b549e1acbe225c45ac3ab63bb925257",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1068e5d2_0cb25f0c",
        "filename": "src/gn/exec_process.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 220,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000402
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T13:37:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure if it\u0027s worth overcomplicating this particular instance given that `pipe2` is not available everywhere and the stdout and stderr pipes already have the same problem today, without close-on-exec at all. This should probably be addressed at https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41202131 by adopting something like [`base::CloseSuperfluousFds`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:base/process/launch_posix.cc;l\u003d216;drc\u003de13869cd76e6f561cb39517715fb640d331b0f9b).",
      "parentUuid": "341d1cbd_6714c9c9",
