      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T03:03:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[AI] The `open(\"/dev/null\")` and `ShuffleFileDescriptors()` failures still `_exit(127)` without writing to `exec_write`, so they still look like the program ran and exited with 127. Consider a small helper that writes `errno` to the pipe and calls `_exit(127)`, used for all the pre-exec failures.\n\nRelated: the result of `base::SetCurrentDirectory(startup_dir)` at line 268 is ignored, so a bad startup dir runs the program in the wrong cwd on POSIX, while on Windows `CreateProcess()` fails and is now reported.",
      "revId": "c54eba3f2b549e1acbe225c45ac3ab63bb925257",
