      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T03:03:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[AI] `WaitForExit()` also returns false when the program was killed by a signal, and by then `std_err` holds the program\u0027s own stderr. So a script that crashes is now reported as \"Could not execute script. When trying to execute \"…/crash.sh\":\" followed by everything it printed, with only the first line indented. This also contradicts the new header comment, which says false means the program couldn\u0027t be started.\n\nCould we either return true with a synthetic exit code (e.g. `128 + WTERMSIG(status)`) so callers take their normal non-zero-exit path, or keep the \"couldn\u0027t start\" reason separate from the captured stderr?",
      "revId": "c54eba3f2b549e1acbe225c45ac3ab63bb925257",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
